# Testing & Local Validation

## Test locations

| Kind | Location |
|---|---|
| Hooks | `src/hooks/**/*.test.tsx` (jsdom + @swc/jest) |
| Components | `src/components/**/*.test.tsx` |
| Platform | `src/platform/**/*.test.ts` |
| E2E | `e2e/*.spec.ts` (Playwright) |

Hook tests wrap with `StoreProvider` via `@testing-library/react` `renderHook`.

Commands: `npm run jest` · `npm run e2e` · `npm run test` · `npm run jest:coverage`

## Mandatory before commit/push (agent policy)

Stop on first failure:

1. `npm run jest`
2. `npm run build`

Run `npm audit --audit-level=high` only when the user asks for audit, or before a release/security change.

## Local SonarQube — only when the user asks

Do **not** run a local Sonar scan for `jest`, `build`, commit, or push.

The scanner has usage limits. Run it only when the user explicitly asks (e.g. "run sonar", "sonar scan", "sonarqube").

When asked:

```
npm run sonar:pr
```

This is a **PR analysis**, the same scenario as `.github/workflows/sonarqube-scan.yml` on `pull_request`:

- Requires an open GitHub PR (or `SONAR_PR_KEY` / `SONAR_PR_BRANCH` / `SONAR_PR_BASE`)
- Target is the PR base (normally `develop`)
- Same host, project key, and `sonar-project.properties` source/test split as CI
- Analyzes **only files changed vs that base** (plus the working tree) — never the whole repo

Do **not** run a bare `npx sonarqube-scanner -Dsonar.projectKey=emporix-showcase`. That is a full-project analysis, is much slower, and counts against scanner limits.

Do not claim local `sonarqube-scanner` equals the pinned GitHub Action SHA in `.github/workflows/sonarqube-scan.yml`.

CI note: PR preview runs `audit → generate → lint → jest` (no build/Sonar). Dedicated Sonar stays in `.github/workflows/sonarqube-scan.yml`.

Husky **pre-push** runs `npm run verify:bugbug-selectors` (changed product TSX must have `data-testid` on actionable controls — see `data-testid-bugbug.mdc`).
